  <downloads>24799</downloads>
  <installedfile>/home/taylor/.local/share/kplymouththemeinstaller/arch-mac-style.zip</installedfile>
  <id>2106821</id>
  <releasedate>2025-09-18</releasedate>
  <summary>&lt;p>Here are some Plymouth Themes, which are inspired by the macOS Boot animation, based on this theme:  &lt;br />&amp;rarr; &lt;a href="https://www.pling.com/p/1805336">https://www.pling.com/p/1805336&lt;/a>   &lt;br />  &lt;br />---&lt;br />  &lt;br />&lt;strong>&lt;em>NOTE: These themes may delay the boot process by a few seconds compared to the default BGRT theme. This is particularly noticeable when the system is installed on an NVME.&lt;/em>&lt;/strong>&lt;br />  &lt;br />---&lt;br />  &lt;br />## Available Plymouth Themes:  &lt;br />&lt;br />- Arch Linux  &lt;br />- Debian  &lt;br />- Deepin  &lt;br />- elementary OS  &lt;br />- Endeavour OS  &lt;br />- Fedora  &lt;br />- Garuda Linux (dragon - red, eagle - blue)  &lt;br />- KDE neon  &lt;br />- Kubuntu  &lt;br />- Linux Mint  &lt;br />- Manjaro  &lt;br />- openSUSE  &lt;br />- Pop OS  &lt;br />- Siduction Linux  &lt;br />- TUXEDO OS  &lt;br />- Ubuntu   &lt;br />- Ubuntu DDE  &lt;br />- Ubuntu Mate  &lt;br />- Ubuntu Studio  &lt;br />- Ubuntu Unity  &lt;br />- Xubuntu  &lt;br />- Zorin OS  &lt;br />- Generic Linux (Tux Logo)  &lt;br />- BGRT (uses the UEFI Firmware background logo)   &lt;br />  &lt;br />---&lt;br />  &lt;br />## Preparation:  &lt;br />  &lt;br />1. The packages &amp;quot;plymouth-themes&amp;quot; and the Cantarell fonts should be installed (system wide) - (for two-step.so (animation) and Cantarell font (for offline-update e.g.))  &lt;br />2. Download the theme, which you like  &lt;br />3. Extract the archive  &lt;br />4. Copy the extracted archive-folder to /usr/share/plymouth/themes/ (sudo/root permission required) - See below  &lt;br />5. Depending on the distribution, the theme needs to be applied - See below  &lt;br />  &lt;br />---&lt;br />  &lt;br />## Installation Examples:  &lt;br />    &lt;br />### Ubuntu/Linux Mint:  &lt;br />  &lt;br />&lt;strong>&amp;rarr; Assuming you want to install &lt;em>&amp;ldquo;ubuntu-mac-style&amp;rdquo;&lt;/em> and the unzipped archive is located in your downloads directory:&lt;/strong>  &lt;br />  &lt;br />Copy the unzipped archive to /usr/share/plymouth/themes/:  &lt;br />&lt;code>$ sudo cp -r ~/Downloads/ubuntu-mac-style /usr/share/plymouth/themes/&lt;/code>  &lt;br />  &lt;br />(Change the name if you want to install a different theme)  &lt;br />&lt;code>$ sudo update-alternatives --install /usr/share/plymouth/themes/default.plymouth default.plymouth /usr/share/plymouth/themes/ubuntu-mac-style/ubuntu-mac-style.plymouth 110&lt;/code>  &lt;br />  &lt;br />With this command, you need to select the theme  &lt;br />&lt;code>$ sudo update-alternatives --config default.plymouth&lt;/code>  &lt;br />  &lt;br />Apply the selected theme &amp;amp; rebuild the initrd:  &lt;br />&lt;code>$ sudo update-initramfs -u -k all&lt;/code>  &lt;br />  &lt;br />---&lt;br />  &lt;br />### Arch Linux/Debian:  &lt;br />  &lt;br />&lt;strong>&amp;rarr; Assuming you want to install &lt;em>&amp;ldquo;arch-mac-style&amp;rdquo;&lt;/em> and the unzipped archive is located in your downloads directory:&lt;/strong>  &lt;br />  &lt;br />Copy the unzipped archive to /usr/share/plymouth/themes/:  &lt;br />&lt;code>$ sudo cp -r ~/Downloads/arch-mac-style /usr/share/plymouth/themes/&lt;/code>  &lt;br />  &lt;br />You need to look, if the system recognizes the theme (if the theme is located in /usr/share/plymouth/themes/)  &lt;br />&lt;code>$ sudo plymouth-set-default-theme -l&lt;/code>  &lt;br />  &lt;br />If the theme is in the list, you can apply this with the following command (Also here, arch-mac-style can be replaced, if you want to use another theme):  &lt;br />&lt;code>$ sudo plymouth-set-default-theme -R arch-mac-style&lt;/code>  &lt;br />  &lt;br />---&lt;br />  &lt;br />### Fedora:  &lt;br />  &lt;br />&lt;strong>&amp;rarr; Assuming you want to install &lt;em>&amp;ldquo;fedora-mac-style&amp;rdquo;&lt;/em> and the unzipped archive is located in your downloads directory:&lt;/strong>  &lt;br />  &lt;br />Copy the unzipped archive to /usr/share/plymouth/themes/:  &lt;br />&lt;code>$ sudo cp -r ~/Downloads/fedora-mac-style /usr/share/plymouth/themes/&lt;/code>  &lt;br />  &lt;br />You need to look, if the system recognizes the theme (if the theme is located in /usr/share/plymouth/themes/)  &lt;br />&lt;code>$ sudo plymouth-set-default-theme -l&lt;/code>  &lt;br />  &lt;br />If the theme is in the list, you can apply this with the following command (Also here, fedora-mac-style can be replaced, if you want to use another theme):  &lt;br />&lt;code>$ sudo plymouth-set-default-theme -R fedora-mac-style&lt;/code>  &lt;br />  &lt;br />Don&amp;rsquo;t forget, to re-build the initrd, if not already done:  &lt;br />&lt;code>$ sudo dracut --regenerate-all -f&lt;/code>  &lt;br />  &lt;br />---&lt;br />  &lt;br />## Additional Information:  &lt;br />  &lt;br />Once the theme has been installed and applied, I hope you enjoy using it.&lt;br />You may need to add some boot parameters, to make the boot animation more &amp;quot;fluently&amp;quot;&lt;br />  &lt;br />Some examples: &lt;code>"quiet splash loglevel=3 rd.udev.log_level=3"&lt;/code>  &lt;br />(These parameters works with Grub and systemd-boot.)&lt;br />  &lt;br />---&lt;/p></summary>
